.superpowers/
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Version-controlled evidence, not scratch: the audit log's line count is a number the
# write-up must report, and an artefact `git clean -xdf` erases cannot be that number. It is
# absent while no holdout read has happened, and tracked from the moment one does.
!data/holdout_access.jsonl

# The comparison ledger, written by the Sink the comparison layer hands its results to (R95).
# MCS membership cannot live in trials.jsonl -- count_trials counts that file's lines, and a
# second kind of record there would corrupt the one number the write-up has to report.
!data/comparisons.jsonl

# The trial ledger, for the same reason: a harness that reports a winner without saying how
# many candidates it considered is the thing this project refuses, and a count `git clean
# -xdf` erases cannot be the number the write-up reports. Append-only, one line per
# evaluated configuration, keyed by the git sha of the tree that produced it.
!data/trials.jsonl

# The agent's own trial ledger (R183). Agent evaluations ARE trials, and a side ledger nobody
# counts is the overclaim this project exists to refuse -- so it is tracked, and the leaderboard
# prints its count beside the headline. It is a SEPARATE file because R139 is a user decision:
# nothing appends to data/trials.jsonl before the user has triggered the holdout reveal. The
# schema is byte-identical to trials.jsonl's, so if the user later rules the two should be one
# file, the migration is `cat`.
!data/agent_trials.jsonl

# The agent's comparison ledger, tracked for the reason comparisons.jsonl is: the MCS membership a
# promotion rests on cannot be recomputed from trial lines, which hold aggregates. Its records add
# `first_origin` and `last_origin`, which comparisons.jsonl's lack -- the gap that forces the agent
# to read no comparison file but its own (design, "the channel M7 closes").
!data/agent_comparisons.jsonl

# The vendor payload archive is committed deliberately, so the repository can rebuild its own
# dataset from a clean checkout: Nasdaq serves only a trailing 10-year window, and anything that
# falls off it cannot be refetched. Narrow on purpose -- the curated, features and targets tiers
# stay ignored, because they are derivable from these payloads. See the Phase 1 spec, section 13,
# and NOTICE for provenance.
!data/vendor_payloads/**

# Editor and OS droppings. Listed because the archive exception above means `git add -A` in this
# repo is no longer harmless -- data/vendor_payloads is tracked, so a stray .DS_Store alongside it
# would be committed too.
.DS_Store
.Rhistory
